  "final_answer": "I have sufficient information from the Google Search results to answer the task. Here is what I found:\n\n## Current Air Pollution Statistics for Los Angeles\n\nBased on Google Search results, the current air pollution statistics for Los Angeles are:\n\n### Overall AQI Status\n- **Current AQI Level: 46** (Good) — according to AQI.in\n- **Status: Moderate** — according to IQAir\n- The difference reflects varying measurement times and stations across the Los Angeles basin\n\n### Pollutant Measurements (from AQI.in)\n| Pollutant | Concentration |\n|-----------|---------------|\n| **PM2.5** | 11 µg/m³ |\n| **PM10** | 20 µg/m³ |\n| **Temperature** | 22.1°C |\n\n### Additional Data (from aqicn.org)\n- **PM10 AQI: 91** (measured by South Coast Air Quality Management District)\n- Ozone (O3) levels are also tracked\n\n### Official Source (AirNow.gov)\n- Los Angeles area is reporting **Good** ozone levels in recent readings\n\n### Sources Referenced\n1. **IQAir** (iqair.com) — LA AQI is currently Moderate\n2. **aqicn.org** — Real-time AQI with PM10/O3 data\n3. **AQI.in** — AQI 46 (Good), PM2.5: 11µg/m³, PM10: 20µg/m³\n4. **AirNow.gov** — Official EPA readings showing Good ozone\n5. **AccuWeather** — Localized AQI and forecast\n\nThe task was completed successfully — Google Search returned the current air pollution statistics for Los Angeles from multiple authoritative sources, showing that air quality is generally in the **Good to Moderate** range today, with the primary pollutant being particulate matter (PM2.5 and PM10).",
